      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-77066",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we find ${g}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\sqrt{t},\\,3\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{t})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9t+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3(t+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(t+1)^{3/2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"
